          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Fuel duty up. Every job starts with a tank of diesel and I cannot pass that on to a customer who is already stretched.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "fuel",
          "when": "below",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "Fuel duty down. On the miles I do, that is real money, every week.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "fuelfrz",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "No fuel duty rise in April after all. On the miles I do, that adds up.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "nicm",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Class 4 National Insurance up. Self-employed people pay it on every pound of profit, and there is no employer to share it.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "vats",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "VAT up. I am VAT-registered, so it is my invoices that go up, and customers who notice.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "ct",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Corporation tax up. I run through a small company like most of the trade; that is my margin.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "cdel",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "More public investment. Half my work is subcontracting on public jobs; when the capital budget moves, so does my order book.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "obr-efo-2026-03",
                "paragraph": "4.12"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "ved",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Road tax is up on the van and on the car. It is not a lot, but it is every year, and it is on top of the diesel.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itbr",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "The basic rate goes up. It comes off the profit on every job.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itbr",
          "when": "below",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "The basic rate comes down. Across a year’s profits, I will notice it.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "nic4",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Class 4 National Insurance up. It comes out of my profits, with nobody to share it.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        }
      ],
      "exposure": ["broad-base", "duties", "business", "motorists", "investment", "nhs"],
      "untouched": {
        "text": "It did not touch the van, the diesel or the invoices. That is a good Budget as far as I am concerned.",
        "sources": [],
        "badge": "simulated"
      },
      "understood": {
        "text": "I got what it was for. Not for me, but I got it.",
        "sources": [],
        "badge": "simulated"
      },
      "puzzled": {
        "text": "Could not tell you. I had the radio on and it was a list of numbers.",
        "sources": [],
        "badge": "simulated"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "professional",
      "who": "A higher-rate professional with savings",
      "fact": {
        "text": "Income tax thresholds are frozen to April 2031, so earnings growth pulls more people into the higher and additional rates each year.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "sourceId": "obr-efo-2026-03",
            "paragraph": "3.2"
          },
          {
            "sourceId": "hmt-budget-2025-document"
          }
        ],
        "badge": "simulated"
      },
      "touches": [
        {
          "code": "ithr",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "The higher rate goes up. On everything above the threshold, which the freeze keeps dragging down towards us.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "obr-efo-2026-03",
                "paragraph": "3.2"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itbrl",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "The higher-rate threshold rises. Less of my pay is taxed at 40%; that is the first time in years.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "govuk-income-tax-rates"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itbrl",
          "when": "below",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "The higher-rate threshold falls. More of my pay at 40%, on top of the freeze.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "govuk-income-tax-rates"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itar",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "The additional rate up. It is a small group paying it, and I am in it.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "it50",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "A 50% rate above £125,000. I remember the last one; it lasted a year.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "legislation-fa-2012-s1"
              },
              {
                "sourceId": "govuk-income-tax-rates"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "cgth",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Capital gains tax up. The savings I built were taxed once when I earned them; now the gains are taxed harder too.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "rvcgt",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "The 2024 capital gains rise reversed. Selling the shares just got a little less painful.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "iht",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Inheritance tax up. It is my parents’ house, and now it is the taxman’s share of it.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "rvinv",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "The dividend and savings tax rises are reversed. The savings account and the ISA both breathe.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "rnrb",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "The extra allowance for leaving the house to the children has gone. The house is most of what there is.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itbr",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "The basic rate goes up. It hits the first slice of my pay, as it does everyone’s.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "itbr",
          "when": "below",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "The basic rate comes down. Everyone gets it, me included.",
            "sources": [],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "pens30",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Pension tax relief at one flat rate. Mine falls, and the pension was the plan.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "hmrc-private-pensions-2026-07-tidy"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "nicuel",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "National Insurance at the full rate all the way up my pay. A pay cut in all but name.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "ifs-green-budget-2025"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "cgtdth",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Gains taxed when someone dies. What my parents leave in shares will carry a bigger bill.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "rf-call-of-duties-2025"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "iinc2",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Another rise on dividend and savings tax. What the savings earn is taxed harder again.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "hmt-budget-2025-table-4-1"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "pens20",
          "when": "on",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "Pension relief at the basic rate only. Mine halves, and the pension was the plan.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "hmrc-private-pensions-2026-07-tidy"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "nica",
          "when": "above",
          "effect": "pays",
          "line": {
            "text": "National Insurance up on pay above £50,270. As a higher-rate taxpayer, I pay it on every pound over.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "govuk-nics-rates"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        },
        {
          "code": "nica",
          "when": "below",
          "effect": "gains",
          "line": {
            "text": "National Insurance down on pay above £50,270. Every pound I earn over it keeps a bit more.",
            "sources": [
              {
                "sourceId": "govuk-nics-rates"
              }
            ],
            "badge": "simulated"
          }
        }
      ],
